<title>INDIA: India's IOC to overhaul data network.</title>
<headline>India's IOC to overhaul data network.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>the Indian Oil Corporation has appointed Price Waterhouse as consultant to restructure its information technology network, a company spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The total project cost is about 300 million rupees,&quot; the spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>State-run IOC is the country's largest crude oil refiner and sole importer of oil. ($1 = 35.80 rupees)</p>
</text>
